## Exterior space (Aussenraum) + fabric (Aussenwand / Fassadenbekleidung / Aussentür / Aussenfenster)

Shared balcony + facade vignette; space card accents the EXTERNAL IfcSpace.
`spaces-exterior` keeps the walk-out terrace only — no BalconySlabUpper overhang;
cladding covers the interior ceiling-slab edge (`cladding_covers_slab`).
Fabric cards omit IfcSpace volumes and accent one product:
Wall accent omits cladding, top slab, upper balcony, and suspended ceiling (open top).
Preview engraves the brand at the top of the accent facade (same as Detailverweis).
Cladding accent omits top slab, upper balcony, and suspended ceiling (open top;
keeps the walk-out terrace — do not reintroduce BalconySlabUpper).
Door accent omits the upper projecting balcony (keeps the walk-out terrace);
cladding covers the interior ceiling-slab edge (`cladding_covers_slab`).
Window accent omits the projecting balcony slabs; cladding covers both
floor- and ceiling-slab front edges (`cladding_covers_slab`, no balcony).
It also cuts a skylight (`SKYLIGHT`, `_add_skylight`) into the top slab: frame
upstand plus a glass plate, accented together with the facade window.

| Concern | Where |
|---------|--------|
| Generator | `generators/exterior_fabric.py` → `generate_exterior_fabric` |
| Shared geometry | exterior vignette in `generators/space.py` (`omit_primary_space`) |
| YAML attrs | `map_exterior_fabric_params` + `WALL_EXTERIOR_*` / `CLADDING_*` / `DOOR_EXTERIOR_*` / `WINDOW_EXTERIOR_*` defaults |
| Samples | `wall-exterior-01`, `cladding-exterior-01`, `door-exterior-01`, `window-exterior-01` |
| Engraving | Wall / door / window: `ENGRAVE_BY_ID` prefer_wall + wall_top. Cladding: `prefer_lowest` |
| Published PNGs | `media/images/{architecture-wall-exterior,architecture-wall-cladding-exterior,architecture-door-exterior,architecture-window-exterior}.png` |

## Interior openings (Innentür / Revisionsöffnung / Innenfenster)

Two-room interior vignette with exterior envelope walls around the slab and an
interior door + window in the partition. Space card (`spaces-interior`) uses the
same flags and drops the camera-facing envelope wall
(`omit_camera_facing_envelope`) so the rooms stay visible. The floor slab
stops on that open plane instead of projecting past it. Fabric cards omit
spaces and accent the door or window. The door card also places a suspended
ceiling over the primary room with an orange `TRAPDOOR` in that ceiling;
the swing door stays visible from the open neighbour room. The trapdoor is
drawn open: a frame lining the cut plus a flap hinged on the camera-far edge,
swung up into the plenum (`HATCH_OPEN_ANGLE`) so it reads as a hatch from above.

| Concern | Where |
|---------|--------|
| Geometry | `_add_space_vignette` flags `include_exterior_envelope` + `include_partition_openings` |
| Generator | `generators/interior_fabric.py` → accents `door` / `window` |
| YAML attrs | `map_interior_fabric_params` + `DOOR_INTERIOR_*` / `WINDOW_INTERIOR_*` defaults |
| Samples | `door-interior-01`, `window-interior-01` (+ refreshed `space-office-01`) |
| Published PNGs | `media/images/{architecture-door-interior,architecture-window-interior,spaces-interior}.png` |

